# Project 4 board (agents)

Canonical policy: [docs/guides/project-board.md](../../docs/guides/project-board.md) (also linked from [docs/issue-tracking.md](../../docs/issue-tracking.md)).

## Non-negotiables

- **Do not** move `Dev Ready` cards to `Backlog` / `Sprint Shaping` to “sequence” the board. Sequence with **Priority** inside `Dev Ready`, or ask.
- **Do not** edit Status or Priority on `In Progress (Product)` (or other Product-owned columns) unless the tech lead **explicitly lists** those issue numbers.
- **No board sweeps** without a proposed change set + explicit approval. Ambiguous = no.
- **Do not merge PRs** unless explicitly asked (Dependabot process is the standing exception when requested).
- **Do not** mutate tickets outside this repo / Project 4 without stopping and per-ticket confirmation — [foreign-tickets.mdc](./foreign-tickets.mdc).
- For the **assigned** ticket only: add to Project 4 if missing; set **`In Progress (Dev)`** on `/start-issue` and **`In PR Review`** when the PR opens (CLI details live in those commands). If **Needs QA**, check **Needs QA? Yes** — post-merge automation moves to `In QA` ([docs/guides/qa-process.md](../../docs/guides/qa-process.md)). If **Needs QA? No**, automation moves to **`Done`** and closes the issue. QA is **not** a merge blocker. Never use closing keywords in the PR body. Do **not** set `Done` on Needs-QA tickets until QA completes.

Tracker: [docs/issue-tracking.md](../../docs/issue-tracking.md). Delivery: [delivery.mdc](./delivery.mdc).
